# docs/calibration/SI4-PROVISIONAL.log — @pixagram/paph-x 1.2.0
#
# SI4-PROVISIONAL: 1.1.2's chain fit (sibench chainfit) re-run on the chain's works hashed in wire 4,
# bound to X3-PROVISIONAL. Quoted by docs/SPEC-SI-paph-si.md (header, §0, §6, §9.8, §10, §11),
# docs/PAPH-X.md §4, docs/SEARCH.md, the README and the CHANGELOG.
# Native, one core of a shared two-core container (Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz), rustc 1.97.0;
# rust/target/release/{sibench,xbench,xcli}, run from rust/; Node 22.22 for the test/ and tools/ scripts,
# run from the repository root. Counts, classes, recalls and artefacts are deterministic and reproduce
# exactly from the same snapshot; timings move by a few per cent between runs, and more when the host is
# busy.
#
# The snapshot is 1.1.2's (docs/calibration/SI3-PROVISIONAL.log, run 0): rust/target/chain-corpus,
# head block 987642, manifest sha256 8d06cb4711e0e1e9c43dabe50edf3ed11039975a17dbc9bfec0afcf1dd27c055.
# The images are not in the repository; no author or permlink appears in the output.
#
# Run 1 is every pair of the chain's 177 works under CAL-007 and CAL-004, XRank under X3 and X2,
# SI3 and SI4. Run 2 fits SI4 (two held-out folds, then all 174 bases); without --out it writes
# docs/calibration/SI4-PROVISIONAL.psi — here a copy, equal to the committed file (the sha256 lines
# after run 4). Runs 3 and 4 are the funnel on the real-base corpus and on the synthetic corpus
# under SI4. Runs 5-7 refit 1.1.1's SI2, 1.1.0's SI1 and 1.1.2's SI3 from the wire-3 caches with
# this release's code: each equals its committed artefact, byte for byte.

